From 9d31a2c5f8b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] backends: skip POSIX shm backend on Android

Android's Bionic target does not expose the POSIX shm_open/shm_unlink API
required by QEMU's hostmem-shm backend. The Android app uses ordinary
file-backed virtual disks and does not require this optional host backend.
Keep the backend enabled on other supported non-Windows hosts.

---
 backends/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backends/meson.build b/backends/meson.build
index 0000000000..1111111111 100644
--- a/backends/meson.build
+++ b/backends/meson.build
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ system_ss.add([files(
   'confidential-guest-support.c',
 ), numa])
 
-if host_os != 'windows'
+if host_os != 'windows' and host_os != 'android'
   system_ss.add(files('rng-random.c'))
   system_ss.add(files('hostmem-file.c'))
   system_ss.add([files('hostmem-shm.c'), rt])
--
2.43.0
